__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Virtualenvs and tool caches, matched as a CLASS at any depth rather than named one
# by one. The narrow ".venv/" + ".audit-venv/" pair let 1.1 GB accumulate unseen in
# sibling and nested environments (dataforge-dbt/.venv, dataforge-dbt/.venv-dbt,
# dataforge-evals/.venv, .venv_bench, plus four nested .mypy_cache trees). Enumerating
# the ones that existed could never catch the next one somebody creates.
.venv*/
**/.venv*/
venv/
.audit-venv/
.env
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.codex_ci_logs/
.benchmarks/
htmlcov/
docs/site/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
.coverage
# Coverage's parallel mode writes one data file per process as
# `.coverage.<host>.pid<N>.<random>`, which the bare `.coverage` pattern above does NOT match.
# Harmless while the suite ran serially; under `-n logical` every worker writes one, so without
# this a parallel coverage run leaves a dozen untracked files a developer could commit. Found
# 2026-08-28 by the working-tree integrity guard, which is what it is for.
.coverage.*

# Editor and agent working directories, moved in from the old parent folder on 2026-08-28 when the
# repository left OneDrive. They are ignored rather than tracked, and each for its own reason:
#
#   .claude/settings.local.json  -- the ".local" suffix is the convention for machine-specific
#                                   settings. A shared `.claude/settings.json` would be trackable;
#                                   this file is not, so only the local one is ignored.
#   .idea/                       -- JetBrains project state. `workspace.xml` alone is a changelist
#                                   and UI layout that the IDE rewrites constantly, and the SDK
#                                   entries name a per-user interpreter registration.
#   .vscode/                     -- editor settings, machine-specific in practice.
#   .snowflake/                  -- Cortex Code's working area. It currently holds 75 plan documents
#                                   (~970 KB) recording past sessions. They are a genuine record and
#                                   may be worth versioning DELIBERATELY, as a reviewed decision --
#                                   not swept in as a side effect of a directory move.
#   .cortex/                     -- the SAME working area under the tool's newer name, holding the
#                                   per-task plan documents. Added 2026-09-14 for the reason above,
#                                   and named separately rather than folded into that entry because
#                                   a renamed directory does not inherit an ignore rule: the old
#                                   path kept matching nothing while the new one showed up untracked,
#                                   which is how a stale ignore rule fails open.
#
# Note `.cursor/rules/dataforge.md` IS tracked, on purpose: agent RULES are shared, agent STATE is
# not. That is the line these entries follow.
.claude/settings.local.json
.idea/
.vscode/
.snowflake/
.cortex/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
prompt.md
compat_output.txt
tmp*.csv

# Session scratch that keeps showing up untracked, ignored for two different reasons.
#
# HANDOFF_*.md -- a bootstrap prompt written to be pasted as the first message of a successor
#   session. It is transient by construction: it pins a HEAD that goes stale on the next commit,
#   so a tracked copy is a document that is wrong more often than it is right. What is worth
#   keeping from one of these belongs in DECISIONS.md, which is the durable record.
# _p.html, _p.txt -- a third-party paper fetched while reading prior art (~1.5 MB of someone
#   else's copyrighted text). Citations belong in PRODUCT.md; the source PDF does not belong in
#   this repository at all.
HANDOFF_*.md
_p.html
_p.txt
DESIGN_PARTNERS.md
.hf-space-stage/
.hf-space-repo/
.hf-space-stage-plan/
.dataforge/canonical_cache/
.wrangler/
node_modules/
playground/web/playwright-report/
playground/web/test-results/
# Locally staged SPA bundle. The image builds its own copy in the web Docker stage; this path
# only exists when running the API directly to check the same-origin serving.
playground/api/web/
data/sft_traj/*.jsonl
!data/sft_traj/.gitkeep
# Paths under archive/ rather than training/: the ML subsystem was excised to archive/training/
# on 2026-09-07, which silently broke these three rules and made seven kaggle_*_kernel/ bundles
# show up as untracked. A stale ignore rule fails open -- it stops hiding things rather than
# erroring -- so a `git add -A` would have swept them in.
archive/training/kaggle/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Generated ML run payloads and Kaggle handoff bundles. Commit compact reports,
# configs, and scripts; keep heavyweight weights/checkpoints local or on HF/Kaggle.
eval/results/**/*.safetensors
eval/results/**/*.pt
eval/results/**/*.pth
eval/results/**/*.bin
eval/results/**/checkpoint-*/
eval/results/**/dataforge-cache/
eval/results/**/dataforge-src/
eval/results/**/runs/
eval/results/kaggle_grpo_candidate_heartbeat_output_*/
eval/results/kaggle_grpo_candidate_v2_probe/
eval/results/kaggle_grpo_smoke_v*/
eval/results/kaggle_grpo_v3_smoke_v*/
eval/results/kaggle_sft_v5_candidate_v*/
eval/results/kaggle_sft_v6_smoke_v*/
archive/training/kaggle_*_handoff/
archive/training/kaggle_*_kernel/

# Per-night input for the cloud automation pipeline; the task changes daily and is
# uploaded to the workspace stage by publish_run_inputs.ps1, not tracked here.
scripts/automation/TASK.md

# Diagnostic output of `dataforge bench --quick`. A reproducibility CHECK must not dirty the
# working tree, and must never be mistaken for the committed multi-seed evidence ledger it sits
# beside: the quick run is one seed, and a positional anchor into it would address a different
# record than the same index in agent_comparison.json.
eval/results/*.quick.json
